[Debug] ----- Vuln Cause Analysis -----
The potential vulnerability is related to command injection. This vulnerability arises because the application accepts user-supplied input in the form of a regular expression for filtering processes, which may be directly passed to system commands without adequate validation or sanitization. If an attacker crafts a malicious input that exploits this lack of validation, they could execute arbitrary commands on the server, leading to unauthorized access or manipulation of the system. This risk is particularly pronounced when the application interfaces with system-level commands like `ps`, as it can expose the server to severe security threats.

